        "raw": "<p>This is not an important question and was, in fact, partially inspired by BrotherDusk&#39;s comment about questions manufactured to keep heads spinning. My question is, when do components played midway through a round get destroyed? For example, if Pillars of Hercules puts one out after six damage has been dealt to Omnitron, does one more damage destroy it or does seven? I see various ways it could go:</p><p>1) Damage-counting for each component begins when it&#39;s played. (I would favour this, but it could require slightly more bookkeeping than the others.)</p><p>2) Begin counting damage for a component once it enters play, but on hitting seven destroy all components, even those that enter play after some of the damage is dealt. (Admittedly, this is probably not the answer.)</p><p>3) Assume damage is being counted every round, and then once seven is hit destroy all components in play, and either a) immediately destroy all components that enter play for the rest of the round, or b) don&#39;t destroy any components for the rest of the round. (One of these is probably RAW, although it could just as easily be either, and RAI may be more geared towards 1.)</p>",
