        "raw": "<p>I see this as being #3. The trigger for destruction is tied to&nbsp;the damage done over a round. When that component comes into play, damage has already happened in the round and I am not sure it&nbsp;can/should be just ignored. After that last 1 damage is done, I would consider the trigger condition as met and destroy the card.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That seems rather straightforward to me. But taking my interpretation of that interaction and extending it possibly creates some weirdness. For instance, lets take the original premise but lets say that 7 damage has already done in the round and that at least one component has already been destroyed because of it. Now Pillars plays a new component during the end of a round in which is has already sustained &gt;7 damage. Does that component destruct instantly? My above interpretation (that I still stand by) would say it does get destroyed, but that does seem a bit odd.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thats how I see it anyway.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
