      {
        "id": 76319,
        "name": "dypaca",
        "username": "dypaca",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-07T14:12:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>While it does seem like it would factor in all damage in the round, I would only destroy a component as a reaction to damage being dealt to Omnitron.&nbsp; So if a component is put into play after 7 damage had already been dealt, I would not immediately destroy it, but I would destroy it when damage of any amount is dealt to Omnitron (that round).</p><p>Note, that while this won't come up alot with Omnitron, it matters a bit more for Rooftop Combat which will typically be played at the end of a round.&nbsp; So long as it is only destroyed as a direct reaction to damage though, it is quite difficult to damage a villain character between Rooftop Combat&nbsp;being played normally&nbsp;and the end of the round.</p><p>Having said that, I think enterpretation 1) is a fine way to play these cards as well.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
